 ### [VoISDF Volume Rendering and Adaptive Sampling](821-voisdf-volume-rendering-and-adaptive-sampling.md)
-VoISDF is a neural volume rendering method that models volume density as a transformed function of a learned Signed Distance Function (SDF) to improve geometry reconstruction and enable adaptive sampling. Unlike prior methods that model geometry as a function of density or use random sampling, VoISDF extracts the surface as the zero level-set of the learned SDF and employs an error-bound-driven adaptive sampling algorithm to avoid salt-and-pepper artifacts without requiring a second network.
+VoISDF is a neural volume rendering method that models volume density as a function of a Signed Distance Function (SDF) to improve geometry reconstruction and enable adaptive sampling. Unlike prior methods that extract geometry from an arbitrary level set of a generic density MLP, VoISDF extracts the surface as the zero level-set of the learned SDF, providing a well-defined surface and inductive bias. It avoids the salt-and-pepper artifacts of random sampling and the density mismatch of second-network inverse sampling by using a theoretical error bound for opacity approximation to drive adaptive sampling.
 
