+Per-Primitive Color Representations define mathematical functions to encode view-dependent color for individual primitives (such as surfels or splats) during rendering. They solve the problem of efficiently parameterizing anisotropic or specular appearance per primitive without relying on global neural fields, allowing explicit texture atlases to recover high-frequency details lost by hash-grid collisions. What sets them apart from sibling methods like [MLP Neural Fields](3854-mlp-neural-fields.md) is the direct optimization of per-primitive parameters (colors, sites, lobes) within an explicit atlas, rather than learning a continuous field via gradient descent through a network.
 
 ### [2D Feature Fusion](2907-2d-feature-fusion.md)
